   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## LTX-2.3 GGUF - long clip / tight VRAM (RTX 3090)\n\nThis is the configuration to reach for when Q4_0 stops fitting.\n\n- **`LTXVSpatioTemporalTiledVAEDecode`** chunks over *time* as well as\n  space. The spatial-only node still allocates the full-length output\n  buffer, so it does not lower the peak for long clips.\n- **`working_device=cpu`** keeps that full-length accumulator in system\n  RAM. Costs a transfer per chunk, buys back GBs.\n- **`working_dtype=bfloat16`** halves the accumulator versus float32.\n- **`LTXVPerStepStatNormPatcher`** runs every denoising step. It was\n  ~181 ms/step of Python loop overhead before this fork vectorized it\n  (now ~6 ms). Do not use it on an un-updated pack.\n\n### If it still OOMs\nLower `temporal_tile_length` first, then raise `spatial_tiles`.\nThe decode now refuses up front with a message naming the shortfall\ninstead of hanging."
   ],
   "title": "Read me"
  }
